hexagon: a start-up self-test of the DSP before the backend registers a device

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

A DSP library can run with no fault and give incorrect values. A v81 library
on v79 silicon gives inf and NaN from each f32 to f16 conversion. Three
kernels that passed the simulator gave incorrect values on v79 silicon. No
silicon of this project verified the v81 library, thus a v81 phone has no
other protection against incorrect values with no error.

The new file htp-canary.h holds the self-test (the canary). The backend runs
it one time, in ggml_backend_hexagon_reg after ggml_hexagon_init, on the
first device, because all devices use the same chip and library. It opens
the DSP session of the device and runs one graph on the op path of the
model:
  - cpy: CPY f32 -> f16 of 4133 values (ties at each exponent, the subnormal
    range, the overflow edge, the signed zeros, the infinities). The bits of
    a nonzero value must be the round to nearest even of the CPU. A NaN gives
    any NaN. A zero gives a zero or an f16 subnormal.
  - q8_gemv: MUL_MAT of a Q8_0 weight in a buffer of the WEIGHTS usage (96
    rows of 512) with one f32 row whose upper 8 blocks are zero, the HVX
    matvec of the decode. The host quantizes the row with
    quantize_row_q8_0_ref and sums the block products in double. The
    tolerance is 1e-5 of the sum of the magnitudes.
  - q8_zero: the same weight with a row of zeros. Each output must be 0 or
    have a magnitude of at most 1e-6.
  - gdn_step: GATED_DELTA_NET of one token, 6 heads of 128, the gates -0.05,
    -1, -6, -88, -1 and -1, the betas 0.9, 0.5, 0.1, 0.7, 0 and 0.5.
    exp(-88) is below the normal f32 range, thus the check finds an exponent
    that wraps. The beta 0 gives a qfloat product by an exact zero before the
    adds of the state update. The reference is the CPU op in double. The
    tolerance is 5e-5 of the sum of the magnitudes.
  - f16_mm: MUL_MAT of an F16 weight (64 rows of 256) with 32 f32 rows, the
    HMX path of the prefill. The tolerance is 2e-3 of the sum of the
    magnitudes (the HMX output is f16).
The zero products: on v79 silicon a qfloat product by an exact zero is not
zero (0.5 x 0 gives 2^-22 as f32), where the simulator gives 0. The v79
silicon runs the model with a KL at the floor, thus the canary permits a
residue of that size and reports it ("zero residue"). A larger residue
fails.

The canary uses graph_compute_async and a synchronize that returns the DSP
status: the synchronize of the backend interface stops the process on an
error status. It catches the exceptions of the session open and of the
buffers. On a failure the registry releases each device and registers no
device, with one error line that gives the first value outside its bound.
The application then uses its other backends. After a pass the first device
keeps its DSP session, thus the model load does not open it again. One info
line gives the result of each check, the open time and the op time.

The switch GGML_HEXAGON_CANARY: 1 is the preset value, 0 skips the canary,
2 runs it and then reports a failure (a test of the path with no device).
ggml_hexagon_init has no canary, thus the fuzz targets of the host that call
it with the fake DSP do not run it.

The phone stage v81 (tools/stages/v81, the OnePlus 13, v79, 2026-09-25):
  - The canary passes in each of 3 runs: cpy 0 of 4133 differ, the zero
    residue is 0 in the cpy and in q8_zero, q8_gemv 0.0121 of its bound,
    gdn_step 0.00366 of its bound, f16_mm 0.0379 of its bound. The session
    open takes 42 to 52 ms and the ops 3.7 to 5.9 ms.
  - The load (the registry and the first open of the device) takes 88.1 ms
    with the canary and 74.7 ms without it (the medians of 3 alternated
    runs each), thus the canary adds 13.4 ms. The session that the canary
    opens is the session of the model.
  - GGML_HEXAGON_CANARY=2 gives no HTP device and the error line.
No v81 silicon verified this patch.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
index 4a17422..6c3a867 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@
 #include "htp/rope-ops.h"
 #include "htp_iface.h"
 #include "htp-drv.h"
+#include "htp-canary.h"
 
 using intvec  = std::vector<int>;
 using uintvec = std::vector<unsigned int>;
@@ -8312,6 +8313,50 @@ ggml_hexagon_registry::~ggml_hexagon_registry() {
     }
 }
 
+// Waits for the pending ops of the canary backend. Returns false when the DSP gave an error status.
+// The synchronize of the backend interface stops the process on such a status.
+static bool ggml_hexagon_canary_sync(ggml_backend_t backend) {
+    auto sess = static_cast<ggml_hexagon_session *>(backend->context);
+    sess->flush_sync();
+    return sess->last_error <= HTP_STATUS_OK;
+}
+
+// Runs the start-up self-test (htp-canary.h) on the first device. All devices use the same chip and
+// the same DSP library, thus one run decides for all of them. On a failure the registry releases each
+// device and the backend registers no device. The first device keeps its session after a pass.
+static void ggml_hexagon_canary_gate(ggml_hexagon_registry * hreg) {
+    if (opt_canary == 0 || opt_ndev == 0 || hreg->devices[0].context == nullptr) {
+        return;
+    }
+
+    ggml_hexagon_canary_report rep;
+    try {
+        ggml_hexagon_canary_run(&hreg->devices[0], ggml_hexagon_canary_sync, rep);
+    } catch (const std::exception & e) {
+        rep.ok     = false;
+        rep.reason = std::string("the DSP session or its buffers fail: ") + e.what();
+    }
+    if (rep.ok && opt_canary == 2) {
+        rep.ok     = false;
+        rep.reason = "GGML_HEXAGON_CANARY=2 reports a failure after the checks";
+    }
+
+    if (rep.ok) {
+        GGML_LOG_INFO("ggml-hex: canary pass on v%d: %s; open %.1f ms, ops %.1f ms\n", opt_arch, rep.detail.c_str(),
+                      rep.ms_open, rep.ms_ops);
+        return;
+    }
+
+    GGML_LOG_ERROR("ggml-hex: canary FAIL on v%d, no HTP device: %s (%s; open %.1f ms, ops %.1f ms). "
+                   "Set GGML_HEXAGON_CANARY=0 to skip the check.\n",
+                   opt_arch, rep.reason.c_str(), rep.detail.c_str(), rep.ms_open, rep.ms_ops);
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < opt_ndev; i++) {
+        delete static_cast<ggml_backend_hexagon_device_context *>(hreg->devices[i].context);
+        hreg->devices[i].context = nullptr;
+    }
+    opt_ndev = 0;
+}
+
 static const char * ggml_backend_hexagon_reg_get_name(ggml_backend_reg_t reg) {
     return "HTP";
     GGML_UNUSED(reg);
@@ -8684,6 +8729,7 @@ static void ggml_hexagon_init(ggml_backend_reg * reg) {
